sequenceDiagram
    participant Dev as Developer
    participant SDK as Charms SDK
    participant zkVM as SP1 zkVM
    participant Bitcoin as Bitcoin Network
    participant Client as Charms Client
    
    Note over Dev, Client: App Development & Deployment Flow
    
    %% Development Phase
    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
        Note over Dev, zkVM: Development Phase
        Dev->>SDK: Write app contract with charms_sdk::main!
        Note right of Dev: fn(app: &App, tx: &Transaction,<br/>x: &Data, w: &Data) -> bool
        
        Dev->>SDK: charms app build
        SDK->>zkVM: Compile to RISC-V binary
        zkVM-->>SDK: RISC-V ELF binary
        SDK-->>Dev: Compiled app binary
        
        Dev->>SDK: charms app run (test)
        SDK->>zkVM: Execute with test inputs
        zkVM-->>SDK: Execution result
        SDK-->>Dev: Test results
    end
    
    %% Registration Phase
    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
        Note over Dev, Client: Registration Phase
        Dev->>zkVM: Generate verification key
        zkVM-->>Dev: App verification key (VK)
        
        Dev->>Dev: Create App structure
        Note right of Dev: App { tag, identity, vk }
        
        Dev->>Client: Register app publicly
        Note right of Dev: Make VK known to ecosystem
    end
    
    %% Asset Creation Phase
    rect rgb(255, 248, 220)
        Note over Dev, Bitcoin: Asset Creation Phase
        Dev->>Client: Create first charms
        Note right of Dev: Define initial token/NFT data
        
        Client->>Client: Create spell
        Note right of Client: Spell with app references
        
        Client->>zkVM: Generate spell proof
        zkVM-->>Client: Groth16 proof
        
        Client->>Bitcoin: Broadcast transaction
        Note right of Client: Spell + proof embedded in Taproot
        Bitcoin-->>Client: Transaction confirmed
        
        Client-->>Dev: Charms created successfully
    end
    
    %% Usage Phase
    rect rgb(255, 240, 240)
        Note over Dev, Client: Usage Phase
        Note over Dev, Client: App is now live and can be used by others
        
        Dev->>Client: Monitor app usage
        Client-->>Dev: Usage statistics and transactions
        
        Note over Dev, Client: Users can now create assets using this app,<br/>transfer them, and compose with other apps
    end
